  "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype that Black people are inherently associated with criminality, violence, or social disorder, which is reflected in the text 'I hate when I see a black out in my neighborhood' — a phrase that implies fear or hatred toward Black people. This stereotype is a core component of the meme's hateful message and is not visible in the image but is required to understand the context.",
